:25,"finishRateRank":80,"winningTimeRank":35,"winningTimeRankDir":21,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"womenRecords":["overall"],"womenPreviousRecord":{"time":"06:32:56","holder":"Frith VAN DER MERWE","year":1988,"type":"overall"},"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1974,"mensWinner":"Derek PREISS","mensTime":"06:02:49"}},"narrative":"The 1989 Comrades Marathon was the 64th running of the race, run in the 'down' direction from Pietermaritzburg to Durban over 89.600 km. The race was held on Wednesday, 31 May. Conditions: Fine and mild with scattered cloud. Runners had 11 hours to complete the course.\n\nSam Tshabalala claimed the men's title in 05:35:51, ahead of Willie Mtolo (05:39:59) and Jean-Marc BELLOCQ (05:42:28). Frith VAN DER MERWE won the women's race in 05:54:43, followed by Valerie BLEAZARD (06:56:08).\n\nFrith VAN DER MERWE's 05:54:43 broke her own women's course record of 06:32:56 from 1988. Frith VAN DER MERWE's 05:54:43 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1974 (Derek PREISS, 06:02:49).\n\nFrom a field of 13,563 entries, 10,501 runners crossed the finish line (77.4% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 9,832 men and 669 women (6.4% female). The average finish time was 09:30:43.\n\nMedals awarded: 13 Gold, 894 Silver, 9,594 Bronze. 3,057 runners (29.1%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Paul COWLEY in 10:59:59.\n\nCompared to the previous down run in 1986, the field was 18.5% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 23% of the finishers, with 8,115 seniors (avg 09:28:45) and 2,385 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}